ain ordinary decay. A finished crop is a real source stock harvested through gather, with its normal energy cost and transfer accounting; nutrition and toxicity apply only through eat. A sustainable supply requires regrowth inputs and surviving plant tissue to remain adequate over repeated actual harvest cycles.\\\\nInterruption and refunds: another action pauses labor; resume rechecks reach, conditions, target survival, access and remaining costs, retaining completed physical work. Cancel ends the work order without undoing soil changes or stopping ordinary plant growth. Death ends the actor's work order but leaves physical plants, soil, litter and any lawful stored materials in the world. No consumed energy, elapsed time, spilled water or completed labor is refunded. Unspent inputs remain where they physically are; return reserved but unconsumed inventory reservations on cancel or death without creating duplicate items. Plant destruction invalidates unfinished work; completed changes remain only where physically meaningful. No other person is made to help, communicate, transfer goods or grant permission automatically. Development and review waiting advance no simulation time. All eligibility, accounting, growth, maintenance, interruption and event rules execute in code, not repeated model review.\\\",\\\"learning\\\":3,\\\"experienceReview\\\":\\\"Study takes three individual simulation rounds; registration, requests, naming, querying and mastery grant no experience benefit. A completed, personally applicable physical trial may yield verified information, including evidence that a suitable-looking plant does not regrow under the tested conditions; record the actual observation and its limits, not universal biological knowledge. Any brief pleasure is optional, event-backed, at most one unit per completed useful treatment, informative trial outcome or harvest, with a ten-round functional-deduplication cooldown; repeated inspections and split work increments do not each qualify. Slowly maintained satisfaction may rise by at most the configured mentalRate 0.04 per round in which independently meaningful practice or participation actually occurs, capped at one unit for this functional cultivation source and decaying by the configured mentalDecay 0.002 per elapsed round. Familiar useful maintenance may qualify without novelty, but idle waiting and ineffective repetition do not. These effects require personal applicability and must use the existing permitted experience channel, not modify protected reward accounts, budgets, goals or permissions. Physical comfort receives no automatic cultivation bonus and remains capped at 10; basic nutrition is unchanged by mood.\\\",\\\"visualReview\\\":\\\"Emit observable events for work started, each physical work increment, paused/resumed/cancelled work, completed soil treatment, observed trial outcome, visible growth-stage change, ripening, harvest transfer and visible damage or death. Reusable visual metadata includes event type, actor when applicable, target/patch ID, location, treatment mode, completed work versus required work, physically visible soil state, observed plant stage and observation time. Use shared patch/plant components with overlays for disturbed soil, removed competition, wilt, growth and ripe produce only when those states exist. Distinguish work completion from successful regrowth and successful harvest. Failed or unfinished treatment must not show a restored-food or ripe-crop success indicator. Private growth eligibility, hidden stocks and unobserved remote changes are not revealed by interface previews or progress bars.\\\"}]}\"}","annotations":[],"logprobs":[]}}

